  "question": {
    "text": "A student performs an experiment to determine young&#39;s modulus of a wire, exactly <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> long, by searle&#39;s method. In a particular reading, the student measures the extension in the length of the wire to be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math> with an uncertainty of <math><mo>&#177;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>0.05</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> at a load of exactly <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math>. The student also measures the diameter of the wire to be<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math> with an uncertainty of <math><mo>&#177;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>0.01</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;The young&#39;s modulus obtained from the reading is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo></math>Take&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>.8</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msup><mi>ms</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>]</mo></math>"
